# Native MLX serving of a local model, on Apple silicon.
#
# Compiled to requirements-mlx.lock with:
#    uv pip compile providers/local_mps/requirements-mlx.in \
#        --generate-hashes --python-platform aarch64-apple-darwin --output-file \
#        providers/local_mps/requirements-mlx.lock
#
# and installed with `--require-hashes` into a private runtime under
# ${HARNESS_ROOT}/.local/runtimes/mlx/<identity>/. It is never installed into the operator's global
# Python, never into a Linux container, and never resolved at launch: the lock's digest is recorded
# in dependencies.lock.json, so a changed dependency set has to be a deliberate commit.
#
# Only the engine library and its own transcriptive deps are listed. The HTTP frontend is served
# from the standard library (`http.server` + `threading`), because adding a framework to the host
# runtime to move bytes between two processes the harness writes itself would be a second
# dependency surface for no capability the platform does not already provide.

mlx==0.32.4
mlx-lm==0.32.2
